{:id "0036-draft-property-fix"
 :title "Fix lab.draft's word-cue property: it discarded half its check and misjudged new letters"
 ;; :lupa/fixes records realized consequence for Lupa's judge scoring: 0026
 ;; shipped a property that never asserted its first check and fails on
 ;; unlucky seeds; found by the foreman when the integration gate failed
 ;; after tick 25 (seed 1793875586231).
 :lupa/fixes #{"0026-lab-draft"}
 :lupa/deps #{"0035-lab-director"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "The gate failed after tick 25 in test/halfahead/lab/draft_test.cljc
        (every-finished-word-is-cued, seed 1793875586231). The
        implementation is correct; the property is not, in two ways:
        (1) its body is a let with two every? expressions and only the
        second is returned, so 'every finished run is covered by a cue and
        every cue's glyphs are live' has never been asserted; (2) its
        word-glyph? model is the set of characters in word-tokens, but the
        random edit ops can cut through surrogate pairs and join halves of
        two different characters into a new one (here D835 from 𝒜 and DE00
        from 😀 made 𝘀, U+1D600, a letter), which the implementation rightly
        treats as a word character and the model calls a non-word. Fix the
        property so it asserts everything it means to, with a model that
        classifies characters the way Unicode does."
 :scope ["test/halfahead/lab/draft_test.cljc"]
 :design "In draft_test.cljc only:
          - Combine both checks with and, so the property returns the
            conjunction (the runs check over every draft along the way, and
            the calls check).
          - Replace word-glyph? with a classification by code point that is
            written in the test (not imported from lab.draft): a glyph is a
            word character when its code point is a Unicode letter or
            decimal digit, or it is ' (U+0027), ’ (U+2019) or - (U+002D).
            On the JVM use Character/isLetterOrDigit on the code point; in
            ClojureScript a \\p{L}|\\p{Nd} regex with the u flag.
          - Add an example test for the failing case: steps \"word\",
            \"𝒜bc😀word\", \"𝘀word\", \"𝘀word \" (all at 0 ms) give a cue on
            the glyphs of \"𝘀word\" and cue-fn calls [\"𝒜bc\" \"😀\"] and
            [\"𝘀word\" \" \"].
          - Run the fixed property with seed 1793875586231 and with 2000
            trials once locally to confirm it passes (do not leave 2000 in
            the file; keep 300)."
 :acceptance
 ["every-finished-word-is-cued returns the conjunction of both checks
   (assert by reading: the let's body is a single and)"
  "The property passes with :seed 1793875586231 and with 2000 trials (say
   so in the final message with the numbers)"
  "The new example test passes"
  "`bb test` stays green on both hosts"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not edit src/halfahead/lab/draft.cljc or any other file"]
 :context ["test/halfahead/lab/draft_test.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/draft.cljc"]
 :budget-usd 6.0}
